dashboard.definition:
{
  "title": "AI Security Assurance: Finding",
  "description": "One finding with its evidence, meaning, mapping, remediation and retest. Opened from a finding row.",
  "defaults": {
    "dataSources": {
      "ds.search": {
        "options": {
          "queryParameters": {
            "earliest": "$tr.earliest$",
            "latest": "$tr.latest$"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "visualizations": {
      "splunk.table": {
        "options": {
          "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
          "headerBackgroundColor": "#0B1F33",
          "headerTextColor": "#FFFFFF"
        }
      },
      "splunk.markdown": {
        "options": {
          "fontColor": "#17202A",
          "fontSize": "default"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "inputs": {
    "input_tr": {
      "type": "input.timerange",
      "title": "Time range",
      "options": {
        "token": "tr",
        "defaultValue": "0,now"
      }
    },
    "input_run": {
      "type": "input.text",
      "title": "Run id",
      "options": {
        "token": "run_id",
        "defaultValue": ""
      }
    },
    "input_ctl": {
      "type": "input.text",
      "title": "Control id",
      "options": {
        "token": "control_id",
        "defaultValue": ""
      }
    },
    "input_hop": {
      "type": "input.text",
      "title": "Hop",
      "options": {
        "token": "hop",
        "defaultValue": ""
      }
    }
  },
  "dataSources": {
    "ds_f_card": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "name": "f_card",
      "options": {
        "query": "`agentsec_assurance_findings_linked`\n| where run_id=\"$run_id$\" AND control_id=\"$control_id$\" AND (coalesce(hop,\"-\")=\"$hop$\" OR \"$hop$\"=\"\" OR \"$hop$\"=\"-\")\n| eval retest=retest_outcome.if(isnotnull(retest_run),\" (run \".retest_run.\")\",\"\")\n| table status_label confidence evidence_class observation interpretation impact control_interpretation recommended_action retest_check retest workshops",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "$tr.earliest$",
          "latest": "$tr.latest$"
        }
      }
    },
    "ds_f_raw": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "name": "f_raw",
      "options": {
        "query": "index=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json \"agentsec.run.id\"=\"$run_id$\"\n| eval seq=tonumber(mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.sequence'),0)), event=mvindex(mvdedup('event.name'),0), hop=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.hop.index'),0), control=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.control.id'),0), decision=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.control.decision'),0), reason=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.control.reason'),0), tool=mvindex(mvdedup('gen_ai.tool.name'),0), attempted=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.operation.attempted'),0), executed=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.operation.executed'),0), boundary=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.trust_boundary'),0), mode=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.testbed.mode'),0), profile=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.security.profile'),0), outcome=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.outcome'),0)\n| dedup seq\n| sort seq\n| table seq _time event hop control decision reason tool attempted executed boundary mode profile outcome",
        "queryParameters": {
          "earliest": "$tr.earliest$",
          "latest": "$tr.latest$"
        }
      }
    },
    "ds_f_frameworks": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "name": "f_frameworks",
      "options": {
        "query": "| inputlookup agentsec_framework_map\n| search control_id=\"$control_id$\"\n| table framework item_id item_name kind relationship rationale verification version_or_date retrieved_on source_url"
      }
    }
  },
  "visualizations": {
    "viz_head": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Finding\n\nPath: **Dashboard, Finding, Raw evidence, Investigation, Workshop, Remediation, Retest.** Every field below comes from the telemetry for this run or from the control catalogue; none is generated by a language model. A lab test is evidence of how a control behaved in the tested environment. It is not proof of organization-wide compliance, certification or regulatory conformance.",
        "fontSize": "default"
      }
    },
    "viz_card": {
      "type": "splunk.table",
      "title": "The finding: observation, interpretation, impact, control interpretation, action and retest",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_f_card"
      },
      "options": {
        "count": 12,
        "wrap": true,
        "rowNumbers": false,
        "dataOverlayMode": "none",
        "tableFormat": {
          "headerBackgroundColor": "#0B1F33",
          "headerColor": "#FFFFFF",
          "rowBackgroundColors": [
            "#FFFFFF",
            "#F6F8FB"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "viz_raw": {
      "type": "splunk.table",
      "title": "Raw evidence: the run's events in order (the hop of this finding is the one the rule judged)",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_f_raw"
      },
      "options": {
        "count": 12,
        "wrap": true,
        "rowNumbers": false,
        "dataOverlayMode": "none",
        "tableFormat": {
          "headerBackgroundColor": "#0B1F33",
          "headerColor": "#FFFFFF",
          "rowBackgroundColors": [
            "#FFFFFF",
            "#F6F8FB"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "viz_fm": {
      "type": "splunk.table",
      "title": "Relevant guidance for this control (educational relationships, not compliance claims)",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_f_frameworks"
      },
      "options": {
        "count": 12,
        "wrap": true,
        "rowNumbers": false,
        "dataOverlayMode": "none",
        "tableFormat": {
          "headerBackgroundColor": "#0B1F33",
          "headerColor": "#FFFFFF",
          "rowBackgroundColors": [
            "#FFFFFF",
            "#F6F8FB"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "viz_how": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "## Reproduce and verify\n\n1. The SPL above (`index=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json \"agentsec.run.id\"=\"<run id>\" | sort agentsec.sequence`) lists every event of the run. Compare the `control.decision` row with any `mcp.started` or `llm.started` row that has the same `hop`.\n2. Open the workshop named in the finding in the Academy (`/learn/lab/<ID>`) or its Splunk dashboard (`ws_lab_*`) to repeat the run: BASELINE, then ATTACK, then RETEST.\n3. After a change, run RETEST again. The dashboards re-evaluate from the new telemetry; the retest outcome on the ATTACK finding changes only when a RETEST with the same attack id and control id shows the control effective.",
        "fontSize": "default"
      }
    }
  },
  "layout": {
    "type": "grid",
    "globalInputs": [
      "input_tr",
      "input_run",
      "input_ctl",
      "input_hop"
    ],
    "options": {
      "backgroundColor": "#F6F8FB",
      "display": "auto-scale",
      "gutterSize": 8,
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 1340
    },
    "structure": [
      {
        "item": "viz_head",
        "type": "block",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "w": 1440,
          "h": 130
        }
      },
      {
        "item": "viz_card",
        "type": "block",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 130,
          "w": 1440,
          "h": 300
        }
      },
      {
        "item": "viz_raw",
        "type": "block",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 430,
          "w": 1440,
          "h": 360
        }
      },
      {
        "item": "viz_fm",
        "type": "block",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 790,
          "w": 1440,
          "h": 300
        }
      },
      {
        "item": "viz_how",
        "type": "block",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 1090,
          "w": 1440,
          "h": 210
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "applicationProperties": {
    "collapsed": false
  }
}
